<body>
<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
<header class="header"><a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="BHIC home"><img src="/assets/7732233b3dc43e88.png" alt="Bugungu"></a><button class="menu" aria-label="Open menu" aria-expanded="false"><span></span><span></span><span></span></button></header>
<aside class="drawer" aria-hidden="true"><div class="drawer__top"><img src="/assets/7732233b3dc43e88.png" alt="Bugungu"><button class="close" aria-label="Close menu">×</button></div><nav class="nav"><a href="/">Home</a><a href="/about/">About</a><a href="/heritage/">Heritage &amp; Museum</a><a href="/visit/" aria-current="page">Visit</a><a href="/contact/">Contact</a><a href="/support/">Support</a></nav></aside>
<main id="main">
  <section class="hero"><img src="/assets/0beb407e817ecb77.webp" alt="Visitors exploring objects inside the Bugungu museum"><div class="hero__copy"><p class="eyebrow">Buliisa · Uganda</p><h1>Come closer to the story.</h1><p>See the objects, hear the living memory and meet the people caring for Bugungu heritage.</p><a class="btn" href="#before">Plan your visit</a></div></section>
  <section class="intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">Your visit</p><h2>A small museum. A much bigger conversation.</h2></div><div class="facts"><div class="fact"><span class="label">Where</span><p>Buliisa, on the eastern shore of Lake Albert, Uganda.</p></div><div class="fact"><span class="label">Best for</span><p>Community members, families, learners, visitors and researchers.</p></div><div class="fact"><span class="label">Before travel</span><p>Please arrange your visit directly with the BHIC team.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="moments"><p class="eyebrow">What you may encounter</p><h2>Objects become stories here.</h2><div class="momentgrid"><article class="moment"><img src="/assets/bae235e9766a12de.webp" alt="A visitor learning about a traditional drum"><div class="moment__copy"><h3>Look closely</h3><p>Everyday objects reveal work, music, belief and memory.</p></div></article><article class="moment moment--text"><div class="moment__copy"><h3>Listen</h3><p>Knowledge lives in people—not only behind glass.</p></div></article><article class="moment moment--text" style="background:#111"><div class="moment__copy"><h3>Ask</h3><p>The richest visit is a conversation, not a checklist.</p></div></article></div></section>
  <section class="plan" id="before"><p class="eyebrow">Before you set out</p><h2>Three simple steps.</h2><div class="steps"><article class="step"><div><h3>Choose who is coming</h3><p>Tell us whether you are visiting alone, with family, a school, a community group or a research team.</p></div></article><article class="step"><div><h3>Agree a date with BHIC</h3><p>The museum is community-run. Contacting the team first helps us give you a meaningful welcome.</p></div></article><article class="step"><div><h3>Come ready to take part</h3><p>Bring your questions—and, if you wish, a memory or story of your own.</p></div></article></div><div class="note"><strong>Do not travel before confirming.</strong><br>Call +256 392 585818 or use the contact page to arrange your visit.</div></section>
  <section class="closevisit"><p class="eyebrow" style="color:#111">Ready when you are</p><h2>Let us know you’re coming.</h2><p>We will confirm the practical details and help shape the right visit for you or your group.</p><a class="btn btn--light" href="/contact/?reason=visit">Arrange your visit</a><p class="micro">Prefer to call? <a href="tel:+256392585818">+256 392 585818</a></p></section>
</main>
